# Gate step 1254-fdsu — measurement producers emit a DOT decimal under a comma
# locale. The fixture injects one chosen by measurement (a GNU-awk-only PATH
# shim adds --use-lc-numeric; BSD awk honours LC_NUMERIC natively) and has a
# mutation arm per producer that strips the LC_ALL=C pins and must go red.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking measurement producers emit dot decimals under a comma locale (1254-fdsu)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-awk-float-lc-numeric.sh"
STEP_ERROR="a measurement producer emits a comma decimal under a comma locale, or a mutation arm went vacuous (1254-fdsu) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Measurement producers emit dot decimals under a comma locale"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-09-26 darwin ok:awk-float-lc-numeric:7"
# ORDER 2155-gpar: runs alone, never beside a sibling step in the gate pool.
STEP_SERIAL="writes fixed-name scratch or mutant files inside the checkout"
STEP_LANES="checkout"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="scripts/freshness-inventory.sh scripts/hooks/pre-commit-openspec.sh scripts/lua/test-awk-float-lc-numeric-signal.lua scripts/refusal-calibration/measure-bands.sh scripts/select-work-batch.sh scripts/test-awk-float-lc-numeric.sh"
